@ThePinkPantha21 Please don't think it is just that simple as your sentence: "...many parents did not financially prepare for their future.  Some couldn't but many just wouldn't."

Go GOOGLE the ups and downs in the economy through the years you were growing up and 30-40 years past that time.  Life is hard!  I remember when raising our children my husband and I both had good jobs/careers but it was so hard to save when everything was so expensive-that's right-expensive because every generation's bills are relative to their salaries so it was just as hard to take care of everything including emergencies back in the 1980's as it is today.  

Nothing has changed in America for the middle and lower class-the rich have just gotten richer.
